#{[17592186061921 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186061923] [17592186061922 :answer/value "9\\operatorname{arccsc} y + C"] [17592186061924 :answer/value "9\\operatorname{arccot} y + C"] [17592186061927 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186061929] [17592186062437 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186062441] [17592186062449 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186062454] [17592186062455 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186062456] [17592186063138 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186063143] [17592186063139 :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsec} x + 6x^{2} + C"] [17592186063143 :answer/value "3\\operatorname{arcsec} x + 12x + C"] [17592186063168 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186063173] [17592186063390 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186063395] [17592186064539 :question/worked-solution "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\text{arcsec}\\,x.\n$$\n\nThen we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{11}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =11\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =11\\operatorname{arcsec} x+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064644 :question/worked-solution "Using $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dy}\\arcsin y=\\frac1{\\sqrt{1-y^2}}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\int\\frac9{\\sqrt{1-y^2}}\\,\\mathrm dy=9\\arcsin y+C.\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on $-1<y<1$."] [17592186064645 :question/worked-solution "Using $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dx}\\arctan x=\\frac1{1+x^2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\int\\frac3{1+x^2}\\,\\mathrm dx=3\\arctan x+C.\n$$"] [17592186064730 :question/worked-solution "The exponential function is its own derivative. Therefore\n\n$$\n\\int3e^x\\,\\mathrm dx=3e^x+C.\n$$"] [17592186064732 :question/worked-solution "For $a>0$ and $a\\ne1$, $\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dx}a^x=a^x\\ln a$. Hence\n\n$$\n\\int4\\cdot5^x\\,\\mathrm dx=\\frac{4\\cdot5^x}{\\ln5}+C.\n$$"] [17592186064733 :question/worked-solution "Integrate each term:\n\n$$\n\\int(2^x-10e^x)\\,\\mathrm dx=\\frac{2^x}{\\ln2}-10e^x+C.\n$$"] [17592186064847 :question/worked-solution "The derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsec}x$ is $\\frac1{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}$ on $|x|>1$. Thus\n\n$$\n\\int\\left(\\frac3{|x|\\sqrt{x^2-1}}+12\\right)\\,\\mathrm dx=3\\operatorname{arcsec}x+12x+C.\n$$\n\nThe constant may be chosen independently on the intervals $(-\\infty,-1)$ and $(1,\\infty)$."] [17592186064852 :question/worked-solution "Rewrite the numerator as $x^2-4=(x^2+1)-5$. Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int\\frac{x^2-4}{x^2+1}\\,\\mathrm dx&=\\int\\left(1-\\frac5{x^2+1}\\right)\\,\\mathrm dx\\\\&=x-5\\arctan x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186064889 :question/worked-solution "Integrate term by term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int(2e^x+4^x-2x)\\,\\mathrm dx&=2e^x+\\frac{4^x}{\\ln4}-x^2+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186069532 :question/worked-solution "To find the general solution, we first separate the variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\sqrt{y} & =2x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =(2x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+x+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the differential equation (in implicit form) is\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{y}={x}^{2}+x+C\n$$\n\nWe're required to write the solution in the form $y=y(x).$ By doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+C}{2}\\right)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse this family on a connected interval where $x^2+x+C>0$. This condition preserves the positive square-root branch used before raising both sides to a power."] [17592186075106 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186075111] [17592186077732 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186077735] [17592186077738 :answer-field/correct #edb/ref 17592186077739]}
